@startuml 02_component_architecture
title Arsitektur Komponen - Supply Chain Microservice
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Klien (POS / Web / Dashboard)" as Client
component "Ferron Web Server\n(TLS, rate limit, reverse proxy)" as FE

component "ms_01 Gateway\n(JWT, RBAC, Routing)" as GW
component "ms_02 Commodity" as COM
component "ms_03 Payment\n(Tunai + QRIS mock)" as PAY
component "ms_04 Retail\n(POS, Stok, Dashboard)" as RET
component "ms_05 Distribution" as DIS
component "ms_06 Warehouse" as WH
component "ms_07 Supplier" as SUP

queue "RabbitMQ\n(exchange: supply.events)" as MQ

database "db_gateway\n(RDBMS)" as DB1
database "db_commodity" as DB2
database "db_payment" as DB3
database "db_retail" as DB4
database "db_distribution" as DB5
database "db_warehouse" as DB6
database "db_supplier" as DB7

Client --> FE : HTTPS
FE --> GW : HTTP (reverse proxy)
GW --> COM : REST
GW --> PAY : REST
GW --> RET : REST
GW --> DIS : REST
GW --> WH : REST
GW --> SUP : REST

RET --> COM : REST (harga & data barang)
RET --> PAY : REST (buat pembayaran)

GW --> DB1
COM --> DB2
PAY --> DB3
RET --> DB4
DIS --> DB5
WH --> DB6
SUP --> DB7

PAY ..> MQ : payment.paid / failed
RET ..> MQ : sale.completed, restock.requested
WH ..> MQ : shipment.requested, po.requested
DIS ..> MQ : shipment.created / delivered
SUP ..> MQ : po.shipped / delivered
MQ ..> RET : payment.*, shipment.delivered
MQ ..> WH : restock.requested, po.delivered
MQ ..> DIS : shipment.requested
MQ ..> SUP : po.requested
note bottom of MQ : Database per service,\ntidak ada akses lintas database.
@enduml
